INTENT: Game Engine 2D

WHEN the developer writes <q:application type="game" engine="2d">
  containing <qg:scene>, <qg:sprite>, <qg:behavior>, <qg:prefab>, etc.
THEN the Quantum parser recognises the qg: namespace,
  builds a Game AST (SceneNode, SpriteNode, BehaviorNode, ...),
  and the GodotCodeGenerator compiles it to a Godot 4 project
  (.tscn scenes, .gd scripts, project.godot) that Godot runs and
  exports to the web, desktop and mobile.

MAGIC:
  - Auto game loop (Godot's fixed physics tick)
  - Kinematic physics (CharacterBody2D, retro console constants)
  - Auto input handling (controls="wasd" → keyboard handlers)
  - Auto camera follow with lerp
  - Auto collision dispatch to behavior functions
  - Auto spritesheet animations
  - Auto sound triggers on game events
  - Behaviors compose on sprites (Unity-style MonoBehaviour)
  - Prefabs instantiate complete game objects
  - FSM state machines auto-dispatch enter/update/exit

NAMESPACE: qg: for game objects, q: for logic/control flow.
